  "id": "adderall",
  "term": "Adderall",
  "definition": "Adderall is a drug made from two synthetic central nervous system stimulants. It can increase wakefulness, concentration, mood, and feelings of well-being, but it also has abuse potential, can lead to psychological dependence, and at higher or prolonged effects may contribute to problems such as hallucinations or delusions.",
